<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">HUMAN GOLD RUSH LESSON</p><h1>Proof of Fulfillment</h1><p class="intro">Technology may record completion, but the human act of follow-through comes first.</p><blockquote>When can a community honestly say, “We followed through”?</blockquote><aside class="notice"><strong>Three QR codes, one moment</strong><p>Every fulfillment moment is captured through three distinct QR codes — Identity, Trade, and Gratitude — inside a 50-meter, 3-minute capture window. The next few years are the “pre-genesis block” period: pattern-testing this capture before any wider rollout.</p></aside></header><section class="content-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h2>One scan, one choice, one event</h2><p>A consented QR interaction creates a pseudonymous, append-only event. The system supplies context so people do not complete long forms.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h2>Two-device handshake</h2><p>Where required, two registered devices confirm the interaction, time window, approved location or proximity, and acceptance outcome.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h2>Final destination</h2><p>A simple yes or no confirms whether an item or commitment reached its intended recipient.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h2>Honest incompletion</h2><p>Promised, attempted, disputed, and fulfilled are different states. Corrections append a new event rather than erasing history.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h2>Identity QR</h2><p>Captures a pseudonymous v-card metadata point at the moment of a scan. It identifies a registered device, never a payment method or financial account.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h2>Trade QR</h2><p>Lives on a “YAM-is-On” sticker or hang tag. Scanning it records pledged community trade value maturing toward the twelve-week window. It is a trading voucher, not currency.</p></div></article><article><span>07</span><div><h2>Gratitude QR</h2><p>The buyer/recipient’s final scan confirms “it happened.” Acceptance, rejection, or no response are each a valid, recorded outcome — and reward Experience Presence (XP) for showing up.</p></div></article></section><section class="media-section"><div class="section-heading"><p>MEDIA FOR THIS LESSON</p><h2>Watch, listen, and discuss</h2></div><div class="media-grid"><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 1</small></div><h3>Proof of Fulfillment: orientation</h3><p>Reserved for the featured story or introductory video.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card video"><div class="media-frame"><span>▶</span><small>VIDEO 2</small></div><h3>Community conversation</h3><p>Reserved for a demonstration, conversation, or local example.</p><a href="#">Discussion guide coming soon</a></article><article class="media-card podcast"><div class="media-frame"><span>◉</span><small>PODCAST</small></div><h3>Listen and reflect</h3><p>Reserved for the facilitator or community podcast episode.</p><a href="#">Transcript coming soon</a></article></div></section>